    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The remainder when $n$ is divided by 6 is 1. This implies that $\\frac{n - 1}{6}$ is an integer. \n\nTherefore, we can express the given condition as follows:\n\n$n - 1 = 6k$ for some integer $k$.\n\nNext, we need to find the expression for $n + 2010$:\n\n$n + 2010 = (6k + 1) + 2010 = 6k + 2011$.\n\nNow we can find the remainder of $n + 2010$ when divided by 6:\n\n$n + 2010 &= (6k + 2011) \\mod 6\\\\\nn + 2010 &= 0 + 1 \\mod 6 = 1$\n\nSo, the remainder when $n + 2010$ is divided by 6 is $\\boxed{1}$.",
